dataSetInformation.common:generalComment:
The module describes the global production mix for ferronickel in 1994. It is designed for the use of the metal as raw material in the manufacturing of stainless steels and alloys. It is not to be used if the impact of ferronickel is considered to be high. In such cases, a more detailed analysis has to be conducted. The data used is mainly based on a study of the energy and material streams resulting from the production of class I nickel. Lacking data mainly on direct process specific emissions were taken form similar processes for copper winning.;
Synonyms: ferro-alloy, Eisenlegierung; 
UUID: 0b63f2b7-3997-3f27-bad0-37025357884e
